`ifndef HISI_GMAC_RDL
`define HISI_GMAC_RDL


regfile eHISI_GMAC {
    name = "HiSilicon GSF gigabit Ethernet MAC with descriptor queues and MDIO";
    desc = "
    HiSilicon \"GSF\" gigabit Ethernet MAC (vendor driver name \"higmac\", the Linux driver is hix5hd2_gmac.c: compatible hisilicon,hi3516a-gmac, hisilicon,hisi-gmac-v2 and hisilicon,hi3798cv200-gmac; vendor U-Boot drivers higmacv300 for the Hi3516A/AV200/Hi3519 class and the older higmac for the Hi3516 V100 class): one 10/100/1000 Mbit/s port (RMII, MII, RGMII; full or half duplex) with an MDIO master, packet counters, a CRF block (flow control of control, IP and broadcast/multicast packets with a 16-entry frame type filter list, TX/RX FIFOs, TSO/SG/checksum offload on the AV200/Hi3519 generation) and four DMA descriptor queues in DDR: RX_FQ (idle descriptors, software writes empty buffers), RX_BQ (RX descriptors written back by the MAC), TX_BQ (TX descriptors written by software) and TX_RQ (recycled TX descriptors), each with start address, depth, read and write pointers, thresholds and a register write-enable (QUEUE_REG_EN) register at 0x500..0x5BC; interrupts are enabled/read/cleared through ENA_PMU_INT, STATUS_PMU_INT and RAW_PMU_INT (0x5C0..0x5C8, write 1 to clear the raw bits); EEE (0x800..0x814) and PMT wake-on-LAN (0xA00..0xA20) exist from the Hi3516A generation on. Unlike the femac (eHISI_FEMAC) and hieth (eHISI_HIETH_SF) Ethernet blocks of the other chips there are no frame FIFOs behind registers: frames are moved by the MAC with its own DMA through the descriptor rings. The data sheets call the block \"GSF\" (gigabit switch fabric, Hi3516A/AV200/Hi3519: two ports on the data-sheet block diagram, but only one port register set and one MDIO) or \"GMAC\"/\"Ethernet\" (Hi3516 V100).
    Variants. The default (no macro defined) is the Hi3516A / Hi3516D / Hi3516A V200 / Hi3519 V101 layout: the four data sheets print the same register set (the register tables of the Hi3516A V200 and Hi3519 V101 are identical, the Hi3516A one differs in one typo only). Define HISI_GMAC_HI3516V100 before including this file for the Hi3516 V100: it lacks DUPLEX_SEL_RGMII (0x08), COL_DISTANCE (0x14), RX_JABBER_ERRORS (0xC4), TX_EXC_COL_ERR_CNT (0x144), TX_TAGGED (0x154), COL_SLOT_TIME (0x1C0), VLAN_CODE (0x1E8), SHORT_ERR_PKT_CNT (0x284), the EEE registers (0x800..0x814) and the PMT registers (0xA00..0xA20), has the extra registers FIFO_THRSLD (0x10), APP_LOOP_EN (0x27C), IP_CHK_ERR_CNT (0x2B4), UDP_CHK_ERR_CNT (0x2B8), TX_RUNT_ERR_PKG_CNT (0x2BC), RX_ERR_TOTAL_CNT (0x2C0), RX_TRANS_PKG_CNT (0x2C8), TX_TRANS_PKG_CNT (0x2CC), RX_BM_OVERFLOW (0x2D0) and MDIO_SCAN_EN (0x3C8), calls 0x344 CRF_RX_ADDR_NUM (CRF_RX_LEFT_NUM elsewhere) and differs in fields: TRANSMIT_CONTROL (an_enable, link_sel), REC_FILT_CONTROL (no vlan_drop_en), CONTROL_WORD (hrdy_sel and other reserved-bit resets), MAC_DA_ADDR_H and CRF_MIN_PACKET (no crf_tx_max_packet / tso_version), CRF_RX_FIFO_THRSLD (11-bit thresholds, other resets) and BQ1_ALFULL_TH (reset 16 instead of 0). The Hi3516 V100 has STATUS_PMU_INT (0x5C8) like the others. The Hi3516 V100 data sheet is the only one that has a Chinese original; no Chinese original of the Hi3516A, Hi3516A V200 and Hi3519 V101 data sheets is available in this workspace (the English editions are used and may carry translation or copy-paste errors; they are noted per register).
    Base address, interrupt and clock/reset. Hi3516A/Hi3516D (hi3516av100, hi3516dv100) and Hi3516 V100: 0x10090000; Hi3516A V200 and Hi3519 V101: 0x10050000 (64 KB window each, data sheet memory map). Interrupt: data sheet interrupt table (Table 3-8) bit 57 \"GSF\" on Hi3516A/Hi3516D, Hi3516A V200 and Hi3519 V101; bit 60 \"GMAC\" on the Hi3516 V100. Clock and reset: PERI_CRG51 (CRG base + 0xCC: 0x200300CC on the Hi3516A/D, 0x120100CC on the Hi3516A V200 and Hi3519 V101): gsf_srst_req bit 0 (GSF soft reset), gsf_cken/gsf_clken bit 1, gmac_if_srst_req bit 2 (MAC_IF reset), gmac_if_cken/gmac_if_clken bit 3 (reset value 0xA: both clocks on), rmii_cksel/rmii_clksel bit 4 (0 CRG clock, 1 pad input), external FE PHY clock select bit 6 (Hi3516A/D: 0 = 50 MHz, 1 = 25 MHz; Hi3516A V200/Hi3519: 0 = 25 MHz, 1 = 50 MHz, the vendor U-Boot agrees) and on the Hi3516A V200/Hi3519 V101 external FE PHY soft reset bit 7 (ext_fephy_srst_req; the vendor U-Boot uses bit 5 for the PHY reset on the Hi3516A, a bit the Hi3516A data sheet lists as reserved); PERI_CRG59 (CRG + 0xEC) is the MAC_IF mode control (port select, speed, RGMII/RMII/MII interface mode) and PERI_CRG60 (CRG + 0xF0) the MAC_IF status. Switching the operating mode (RMII 10/100 or RGMII 10/100/1000): set PERI_CRG51 to 0xE (reset), write PERI_CRG59 bits 8:0, set PERI_CRG51 to 0xA, then program MODE_CHANGE_EN = 1, PORT_MODE, MODE_CHANGE_EN = 0 (data sheet 5.4.6; the same sequence is in Linux and the vendor U-Boot). Hi3516 V100: PERI_CRG21 (0x20030054): gmac_rst_req bit 0, gmac_cken bit 1, gmac_txclk_mode bits 5:4 (MII / RGMII 10, 100, 1000 Mbit/s); the older vendor U-Boot driver higmac programs it as PERI_CRG21.
    Descriptors (data sheet 5.4.2): word 0 = packet buffer address, word 1 = hw_own / sg_flag / coe_flag / tso_flag / data_len / vlan and IP header fields (Table 5-2); the queue depth registers count words, not descriptors; the maximum RX frame length is 1.6 KB, the drivers use 1600 byte frames in 1728 byte buffers and 32 byte descriptors.
    Register names, offsets, resets and field descriptions are from the Hi3516A V200 data sheet issue 01 (2018-07-05), chapter 5 (printed pages 5-17..5-109, section 5.6 summary at text dump line 30283, section 5.7 descriptions at lines 30690-35983, file Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt); the Hi3516A/Hi3516D data sheet issue 01 (2016-10-28; summary 50835, descriptions 51241-56448), the Hi3519 V101 data sheet (summary 30218, descriptions 30625-35918) and the Hi3516 V100 data sheet issue 00B60 (2011-08-12, Chinese; summary 28426, descriptions 28895-34678) were compared register by register and field by field (the three English editions are identical apart from the register and the field descriptions in one sentence of TX_BQ_RD_ADDR; the V100 differences are the variant above). The V100-only registers are translated from the Chinese text. The summary table and the register headers of the data sheet contain several errors that were corrected as noted per register (the registers at 0xC8 and 0xCC are only in the summary table and in a block directly after RX_JABBER_ERRORS; the FILTER_LIST register has no summary row; RX_FQ_ALRMPTY_TH is spelled ALRMPTY; PMT_CTRL_STAUTS is spelled STAUTS). Cross-checked against Linux hix5hd2_gmac.c (every offset, bit mask and access pattern it defines agrees; it additionally names RX_CFF_NUM_REG 0x5F0, PMU_FSM_REG 0x5F8, RX_FIFO_PKT_IN_NUM 0x5FC and RX_FIFO_PKT_OUT_NUM 0x600, which no data sheet describes and the driver never uses, so they are not modelled) and the vendor U-Boot higmacv300 and higmac headers (offsets agree; the FLUSH_CMD bit layout and the PHY address mask differ, see FLUSH_CMD and MDIO_SINGLE_CMD). The vendor U-Boot also writes 0xE to GSF offset 0x3004 (\"CRF ack threshold\" of the dual-MAC variant), which is outside the documented registers. Not hardware verified.
";

    reg {
        name = "Local MAC address register";
        desc = "STATION_ADDR_LOW is a local MAC address register.

Vendor U-Boot (higmac_hw_set_macaddress) writes STATION_ADDR_HIGH (bits 15:0 = MAC bytes 0 and 1) and then STATION_ADDR_LOW (bytes 2..5).

Data sheet 5.7 STATION_ADDR_LOW (offset 0x0, printed page 5-17, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 30695).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 STATION_ADDR_LOW (offset 0x0, printed page 5-18, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 28910).";

        field {
            name = "station_addr_low";
            desc = "Lower 32 bits for the source MAC address of MAC_CORE";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } station_addr_low[31:0];
    } STATION_ADDR_LOW @ 0x0;

    reg {
        name = "Local MAC address register";
        desc = "STATION_ADDR_HIGH is a local MAC address register.

Data sheet 5.7 STATION_ADDR_HIGH (offset 0x4, printed page 5-17, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 30714).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 STATION_ADDR_HIGH (offset 0x4, printed page 5-18, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 28929).";

        field {
            name = "station_addr_high";
            desc = "Upper 16 bits of the source MAC address of MAC_CORE. The default configurations can be used.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } station_addr_high[15:0];
    } STATION_ADDR_HIGH @ 0x4;

`ifndef HISI_GMAC_HI3516V100
    reg {
        name = "Half-duplex selection register";
        desc = "DUPLEX_SEL_RGMII is a half-duplex selection register.

Linux hix5hd2_gmac.c calls this register MAC_DUPLEX_HALF_CTRL and writes the duplex flag (1 = full) after programming PORT_MODE; the vendor U-Boot (higmac.c) writes 0 (half) or 1 (full). Not present on the Hi3516 V100.

Data sheet 5.7 DUPLEX_SEL_RGMII (offset 0x8, printed page 5-18, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 30746).";

        enum DUPLEX_SEL_RGMII_duplex_sel_rgmii_enum {
            HALF_DUPLEX = 0 { name = "Half Duplex"; desc = "half duplex"; };
            FULL_DUPLEX = 1 { name = "Full Duplex"; desc = "full duplex"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "duplex_sel_rgmii";
            desc = "Half-duplex selection signal";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = DUPLEX_SEL_RGMII_duplex_sel_rgmii_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } duplex_sel_rgmii[0:0];
    } DUPLEX_SEL_RGMII @ 0x8;
`endif

    reg {
        name = "Flow control frame type domain register";
        desc = "FD_FC_TYPE is a flow control frame type domain register.

Data sheet 5.7 FD_FC_TYPE (offset 0xC, printed page 5-18, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 30774).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 FD_FC_TYPE (offset 0xC, printed page 5-18, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 28950).";

        field {
            name = "fd_fc_type";
            desc = "Flow control frame type domain in full-duplex mode";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x8808;
        } fd_fc_type[15:0];
    } FD_FC_TYPE @ 0xC;

`ifdef HISI_GMAC_HI3516V100
    reg {
        name = "MAC application-side FIFO parameter setting register";
        desc = "FIFO_THRSLD is the MAC application-side FIFO parameter setting register.

Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 FIFO_THRSLD (offset 0x10, printed page 5-19, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 28977). Hi3516 V100 only (not in the Hi3516A, Hi3516A V200 and Hi3519 V101 data sheets).";

        field {
            name = "thrsld_inter_clock";
            desc = "Application-side FIFO parameter that defines the ratio between the FIFO read and write clocks.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } thrsld_inter_clock[31:24];

        field {
            name = "thrsld_for_p_empty";
            desc = "Application-side FIFO parameter that defines the low watermark of the FIFO.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0xA;
        } thrsld_for_p_empty[23:16];

        field {
            name = "thrsld_for_p_full";
            desc = "Application-side FIFO parameter that defines the high watermark of the FIFO. The user must not modify it.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x19;
        } thrsld_for_p_full[15:8];

        field {
            name = "buff_sz_for_tsmt";
            desc = "Application-side FIFO parameter that defines the threshold for starting a read operation of the FIFO.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x10;
        } buff_sz_for_tsmt[7:0];
    } FIFO_THRSLD @ 0x10;
`endif

`ifndef HISI_GMAC_HI3516V100
    reg {
        name = "Single retransmission packet length threshold register";
        desc = "COL_DISTANCE is a single retransmission packet length threshold register.

Data sheet 5.7 COL_DISTANCE (offset 0x14, printed page 5-19, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 30799).";

        field {
            name = "col_distance";
            desc = "Single retransmission packet length threshold";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x43;
        } col_distance[9:0];
    } COL_DISTANCE @ 0x14;
`endif

    reg {
        name = "Flow control time parameter register";
        desc = "FC_TX_TIMER is a flow control time parameter register.

Data sheet 5.7 FC_TX_TIMER (offset 0x1C, printed page 5-19, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 30819).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 FC_TX_TIMER (offset 0x1C, printed page 5-19, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 29004).";

        field {
            name = "fc_tx_timer";
            desc = "Parameter of the time period during which flow control frames are transmitted. The unit of the time period is measured by how long 512 bits are transmitted. In 100 Mbit/s mode, the unit is equivalent to 128 clock periods. In 1000 Mbit/s mode, the unit is equivalent to 64 clock periods.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0xFF;
        } fc_tx_timer[15:0];
    } FC_TX_TIMER @ 0x1C;

    reg {
        name = "Flow control frame destination address lower 32 bits register";
        desc = "FD_FC_ADDR_LOW is a flow control frame destination address lower 32 bits register.

Data sheet 5.7 FD_FC_ADDR_LOW (offset 0x20, printed page 5-20, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 30851).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 FD_FC_ADDR_LOW (offset 0x20, printed page 5-20, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 29037).";

        field {
            name = "fd_fc_addr_low";
            desc = "Lower 32 bits of the destination address of the flow control frame";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0xC2000001;
        } fd_fc_addr_low[31:0];
    } FD_FC_ADDR_LOW @ 0x20;

    reg {
        name = "Flow control frame destination address upper 16 bits register";
        desc = "FD_FC_ADDR_HIGH is a flow control frame destination address upper 16 bits register.

Data sheet 5.7 FD_FC_ADDR_HIGH (offset 0x24, printed page 5-20, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 30869).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 FD_FC_ADDR_HIGH (offset 0x24, printed page 5-20, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 29056).";

        field {
            name = "fd_fc_addr_high";
            desc = "Upper 16 bits of the destination address of the flow control frame";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x180;
        } fd_fc_addr_high[15:0];
    } FD_FC_ADDR_HIGH @ 0x24;

    reg {
        name = "TX frame inter-packet gap (IPG) register";
        desc = "IPG_TX_TIMER is a TX frame IPG register.

Data sheet 5.7 IPG_TX_TIMER (offset 0x30, printed page 5-20, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 30889).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 IPG_TX_TIMER (offset 0x30, printed page 5-20, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 29077).";

        field {
            name = "ipg_tx_timer";
            desc = "TX frame IPG, in the unit of byte";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x8;
        } ipg_tx_timer[7:0];
    } IPG_TX_TIMER @ 0x30;

    reg {
        name = "TX flow control frame IPG register";
        desc = "PAUSE_THR is a TX flow control frame IPG register.

Data sheet 5.7 PAUSE_THR (offset 0x38, printed page 5-21, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 30913).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 PAUSE_THR (offset 0x38, printed page 5-21, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 29104).";

        field {
            name = "pause_thr";
            desc = "IPG of the flow control frame. If the flow control time is longer than the IPG, the MAC transmits the flow control frame automatically. The unit of the time period is measured by how long 512 bits are transmitted. In 100 Mbit/s mode, the unit is equivalent to 128 clock periods. In 1000 Mbit/s mode, the unit is equivalent to 64 clock periods.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x2F;
        } pause_thr[15:0];
    } PAUSE_THR @ 0x38;

    reg {
        name = "Maximum frame length register";
        desc = "MAX_FRM_SIZE is a maximum frame length register.

Linux/U-Boot: the field is 14 bits wide (BITS_MAX_FRM_SIZE = bits 13:0).

Data sheet 5.7 MAX_FRM_SIZE (offset 0x3C, printed page 5-21, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 30938).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 MAX_FRM_SIZE (offset 0x3C, printed page 5-21, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 29129).";

        field {
            name = "max_frm_size";
            desc = "Maximum frame length on the MAC side If the length of an RX frame is greater than the maximum length, the RX frame is regarded as an oversized frame. When the length of a frame to be transmitted is greater than the maximum length, the frame is broken up and then transmitted as an error frame.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x5EE;
        } max_frm_size[13:0];
    } MAX_FRM_SIZE @ 0x3C;

    reg {
        name = "Port status register";
        desc = "PORT_MODE is a port status register.

Linux hix5hd2_gmac.c and the vendor U-Boot write 0 (10M), 1 (100M) or 5 (1000M) here between writes of 1 and 0 to MODE_CHANGE_EN (the MAC_IF mode and duplex are programmed separately in the CRG register PERI_CRG59). The vendor U-Boot names the values PORT_MOD_*.

Data sheet 5.7 PORT_MODE (offset 0x40, printed page 5-22, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 30967).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 PORT_MODE (offset 0x40, printed page 5-22, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 29164).";

        enum PORT_MODE_port_mode_enum {
            SPEED_10M = 0 { name = "10 Mbit/s"; desc = "10 Mbit/s"; };
            SPEED_100M = 1 { name = "100 Mbit/s"; desc = "100 Mbit/s"; };
            SPEED_1000M = 5 { name = "1000 Mbit/s"; desc = "1000 Mbit/s (other values are reserved)"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "port_mode";
            desc = "Current MAC port mode";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PORT_MODE_port_mode_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } port_mode[2:0];
    } PORT_MODE @ 0x40;

    reg {
        name = "Channel enable register";
        desc = "PORT_EN is a channel enable register.

Linux BITS_TX_EN = bit 2 and BITS_RX_EN = bit 1; the reset value 0x6 has both channels enabled.

Data sheet 5.7 PORT_EN (offset 0x44, printed page 5-22, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 30995).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 PORT_EN (offset 0x44, printed page 5-22, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 29199).";

        enum PORT_EN_tx_en_enum {
            DISABLED = 0 { name = "Disabled"; desc = "disabled"; };
            ENABLED = 1 { name = "Enabled"; desc = "enabled"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "tx_en";
            desc = "TX channel enable";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PORT_EN_tx_en_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } tx_en[2:2];

        enum PORT_EN_rx_en_enum {
            DISABLED = 0 { name = "Disabled"; desc = "disabled"; };
            ENABLED = 1 { name = "Enabled"; desc = "enabled"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "rx_en";
            desc = "RX channel enable";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PORT_EN_rx_en_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } rx_en[1:1];
    } PORT_EN @ 0x44;

    reg {
        name = "Flow control enable register";
        desc = "PAUSE_EN is a flow control enable register.

Data sheet 5.7 PAUSE_EN (offset 0x48, printed page 5-23, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 31032).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 PAUSE_EN (offset 0x48, printed page 5-23, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 29241).";

        field {
            name = "reserved_nz";
            desc = "Reserved (RO); reads 1: the data sheet total reset value is 0x0000_0007 although only bits 1:0 are described (identical in all data sheet editions; not read on hardware).";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            reset = 0x1;
        } reserved_nz[2:2];

        enum PAUSE_EN_tx_fdfc_enum {
            DISABLED = 0 { name = "Disabled"; desc = "disabled"; };
            ENABLED = 1 { name = "Enabled"; desc = "enabled"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "tx_fdfc";
            desc = "Flow control frame transmit enable in full-duplex mode";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PAUSE_EN_tx_fdfc_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } tx_fdfc[1:1];

        enum PAUSE_EN_rx_fdfc_enum {
            DISABLED = 0 { name = "Disabled"; desc = "disabled"; };
            ENABLED = 1 { name = "Enabled"; desc = "enabled"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "rx_fdfc";
            desc = "Flow control frame response enable in full-duplex mode";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PAUSE_EN_rx_fdfc_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } rx_fdfc[0:0];
    } PAUSE_EN @ 0x48;

    reg {
        name = "Short frame threshold register";
        desc = "SHORT_RUNTS_THR is a short frame threshold register.

Data sheet 5.7 SHORT_RUNTS_THR (offset 0x50, printed page 5-23, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 31060).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 SHORT_RUNTS_THR (offset 0x50, printed page 5-23, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 29270).";

        field {
            name = "short_runts_thr";
            desc = "Short frame threshold (for statistics only)";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0xC;
        } short_runts_thr[4:0];
    } SHORT_RUNTS_THR @ 0x50;

    reg {
        name = "Drop enable register for unknown control frames";
        desc = "DROP_UNK_CTL_FRM is a drop enable register for unknown control frames.

Data sheet 5.7 DROP_UNK_CTL_FRM (offset 0x54, printed page 5-24, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 31085).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 DROP_UNK_CTL_FRM (offset 0x54, printed page 5-24, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 29300).";

        enum DROP_UNK_CTL_FRM_drop_unk_ctl_frm_enum {
            FORWARD = 0 { name = "Forward"; desc = "The unknown control frames are forwarded normally."; };
            DROP = 1 { name = "Drop"; desc = "The unknown control frames are dropped."; };
        };

        field {
            name = "drop_unk_ctl_frm";
            desc = "Processing method of the unknown control frames";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = DROP_UNK_CTL_FRM_drop_unk_ctl_frm_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } drop_unk_ctl_frm[0:0];
    } DROP_UNK_CTL_FRM @ 0x54;

    reg {
        name = "Common configuration register";
        desc = "TRANSMIT_CONTROL is a common configuration register.

Data sheet 5.7 TRANSMIT_CONTROL (offset 0x60, printed page 5-24, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 31114).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 TRANSMIT_CONTROL (offset 0x60, printed page 5-24, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 29330).";

        enum TRANSMIT_CONTROL_pad_enable_enum {
            DISABLED = 0 { name = "Disabled"; desc = "disabled"; };
            ENABLED = 1 { name = "Enabled"; desc = "enabled"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "pad_enable";
            desc = "PAD addition enable";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = TRANSMIT_CONTROL_pad_enable_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } pad_enable[7:7];

        enum TRANSMIT_CONTROL_crc_add_enum {
            ENABLED = 0 { name = "Enabled"; desc = "enabled"; };
            DISABLED = 1 { name = "Disabled"; desc = "disabled"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "crc_add";
            desc = "FCS addition enable";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = TRANSMIT_CONTROL_crc_add_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } crc_add[6:6];

`ifdef HISI_GMAC_HI3516V100
        field {
            name = "an_enable";
            desc = "Auto-negotiation enable. 0: disabled, fixed configuration; 1: enabled. (Hi3516 V100 data sheet, Chinese original; read-only there.)";
