    reg {
        name = "PMU raw interrupt status register";
        desc = "RAW_PMU_INT is a PMU raw interrupt status register.

The data sheet lists the bits as RW with the text \"cleared by writing 1 to this bit\"; Linux hix5hd2_gmac.c (writel(ints, RAW_PMU_INT), writel(~0, ...)) and the vendor U-Boot (higmac_clear_irqstatus) clear it by writing 1 (write-1-to-clear); the bit assignment equals the ENA_PMU_INT/STATUS_PMU_INT bit assignment and the Linux *_INT masks. Linux DEF_INT_MASK enables RX_BQ_IN_INT, RX_BQ_IN_TIMEOUT_INT, TX_RQ_IN_INT and TX_RQ_IN_TIMEOUT_INT (bits 17, 28, 19, 29).

Data sheet 5.7 RAW_PMU_INT (offset 0x5C0, printed page 5-83, `Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 34449).
Hi3516 V100 data sheet (Chinese original) 5.6 RAW_PMU_INT (offset 0x5C0, printed page 5-95, `Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 33602).";

